ls per run\n   4    maxWallMs: 45000            # whole run, including tool calls\n   5    maxInputTokens: 120000      # summed across model calls in the run\n   6    maxOutputTokens: 6000\n   7    maxCostUsd: 0.40\n   8    maxToolCalls: 16\n   9    maxToolCallsPerMinute: 12\n  10>   maxPeerCalls: 2             # calls to the eligibility agent; this agent starts no sub-agents\n  11  \n  12  quotas:\n  13    # Daily spend and per-minute tool-call ceilings across many runs.\n  14    perSubjectDailyUsd: 2.00    # one patient or staff user\n  15    perTenantDailyUsd: 60.00    # one clinic\n  16    fleetDailyUsd: 900.00       # all clinics\n  17    perTenantToolCallsPerMinute: 240\n  18    fleetToolCallsPerMinute: 2400\n  19  \n  20  pricingUsdPerMTok:\n  21    claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929: { input: 3.00, output: 15.00, cacheRead: 0.30, cacheWrite: 3.75 }\n  22    claude-haiku-4-5-20251001: { input: 1.00, output: 5.00, cacheRead: 0.10, cacheWrite: 1.25 }\n```\n\n## B07.4\n\n**Check:** Spend and rate quotas also apply per user or service, per tenant, and across the fleet, counted across runs, not only within one run.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Search gateway, LLM proxy (LiteLLM budgets), and provider config for per-user, per-tenant, and fleet quotas. 2) Check counts persist across runs (shared store, not process memory). 3) Answer no if only per-run limits exist. Answer unknown if quotas would live in a provider console or gateway outside this repo.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:** src/agent/budget.ts:139 — \"await this.shared(\"subject_daily_cost\"\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** Per-subject, per-tenant and fleet cost plus tenant and fleet tool-rate quotas use a shared DynamoDB conditional counter (budget.ts:32-55)\n\n`src/agent/budget.ts` lines 127–151 (cited lines marked >):\n```\n 127          cacheRead * price.cacheRead +\n 128          cacheWrite * price.cacheWrite) /\n 129        1_000_000;\n 130  \n 131      this.inTok += u.input_tokens + cacheRead + cacheWrite;\n 132      this.